{"name":"Lime Slice","hex":"#f0fded","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"},{"term":"slice","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is thin and broad.","A thin, broad piece cut off."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cut into slices.","To cut with an edge using a drawing motion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slice"}],"entries":[{"title":"Slice (drink)","blocks":[{"text":"Slice is a line of primarily fruit-flavored soft drinks originally manufactured by PepsiCo and currently manufactured as a low-sugar prebiotic soda by Suja Life. Slice was first introduced in 1984 but discontinued by PepsiCo in North America in the late 2000s."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/02/Slice_drink_brand_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slice_(drink)","wikidata":"Q7540223"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(